{{!-- THE SHEET-FACE STRIP — the first thing on every vehicle face, and the same control on all of
     them, so any face can reach any other (returning to the standard sheet is simply picking
     Standard). Deliberately its own labelled strip above the header rather than a checkbox among
     the identity fields: it selects the whole layout, not one of the vehicle's stats.

     ⭐ SHARED BY TWO DOCUMENT TYPES. The vehicle ACTOR's three faces include it, and so does the
     vehicle ITEM sheet, where the same designation says which face a deploy from that pink slip
     opens on. Everything the strip needs arrives in `faceControl` — including its own element id —
     so the partial never reaches for `actor` or `item` and reads the same on both.

     Offered on EVERY vehicle sheet (user ruling 2026-08-25). It used to be withheld from
     compendium-deployed vehicles; class/provenance derivation now only chooses the DEFAULT
     selection when nothing is designated (module/vehicle/vehicle-face.js).

     The select carries NO `name`: it is not one stored field. Picking an option writes the pair
     {isACPA, isMMVehicle} atomically through the sheet's own handler. --}}
{{#if faceControl.show}}
<div class="cp-veh-face-strip" title="{{CPLocal 'Vehicle.FaceTip'}}">
    <label class="cp-veh-face-label" for="cp-veh-face-{{faceControl.domId}}">{{CPLocal "Vehicle.FaceLabel"}}</label>
    <select class="cp-veh-face-select" id="cp-veh-face-{{faceControl.domId}}"
            data-face-current="{{faceControl.value}}" {{#if faceControl.locked}}disabled{{/if}}>
        {{#each faceControl.options}}
        <option value="{{value}}" {{#if selected}}selected{{/if}} {{#if disabled}}disabled{{/if}}>{{label}}</option>
        {{/each}}
    </select>
    {{#if faceControl.mmGated}}
    {{!-- The breadcrumb: the MM option stays VISIBLE and disabled, and this line names the world
          setting the path runs through, so the gate can be learned from the sheet. --}}
    <span class="cp-veh-face-hint">{{CPLocal "Vehicle.FaceMMGateHint"}}</span>
    {{/if}}
    {{#if faceControl.derivedOnly}}
    {{!-- Nothing designated: the option shown was read off the vehicle's own class, not recorded.
          Its own line and its own class so the world-gate breadcrumb above can be asserted
          separately from this one. The face it is showing is NAMED in the line (`chosenLabel`, the
          same localized option label the select carries) — the earlier wording said only "the sheet
          the vehicle's own class calls for", which the user read as a statement about the class
          rather than about which sheet was on screen. --}}
    <span class="cp-veh-face-derived">{{CPLocal "Vehicle.FaceDerivedHint" sheet=faceControl.chosenLabel}}</span>
    {{/if}}
</div>
{{/if}}
